issue(id="0015" status="open")
  title Add configurable text-payload whitespace compaction with opt-out control
  user-story
    as-a maintainer of puggers
    i-want a configurable policy for compacting repeated spaces and tabs inside text payloads
    so-that teams can use tighter default output while still disabling the behavior where authored text spacing must be preserved
  premise.
    The current formatter policy intentionally distinguishes structural
    whitespace from text payload whitespace. That keeps authored text safe in
    Pug contexts where repeated spaces or tabs may still be meaningful, but it
    leaves open a future policy for projects that want more aggressive cleanup
    in prose-like content. Any such behavior should have explicit configuration,
    should default to the formatter's preferred behavior unless opted out, and
    should document its rendering assumptions while avoiding whitespace-
    preserving regions such as preformatted output, raw text blocks, or other
    contexts where repeated spacing is intended content.
  acceptance-criteria
    criterion Define the exact scope of text-payload whitespace compaction, including which Pug text contexts are eligible by default and which must remain untouched.
    criterion Add focused fixtures showing safe cases, unsafe cases, and ambiguous cases for repeated spaces and tabs between words.
    criterion Specify the user-facing configuration shape and the default behavior, making clear how projects opt out when authored spacing should win.
    criterion Document the rendering assumptions and risks, including HTML whitespace collapse versus preserved-whitespace contexts such as preformatted output or CSS white-space controls.
  review-items
    item(status="open") Decide whether the option belongs in the formatter core, the importer, or both.
    item(status="open") Confirm whether the default-enabled behavior should begin with plain inline text only before considering piped lines, dotted prose, or broader block-text contexts.
